n County","/arc-plc/pennsylvania/huntingdon-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 10 grids runs 75 years back to 1951, and September to October came in under 90% of normal in 34 of them, more than any other pair. In 2025 the middle of the grids got 166% of normal in May to June but just 47% in August to September. So far in 2026, June to July is at 125% of normal on the middle of the grids. Grid 24210 had its driest year in 2001 at 65% of normal.</p>"}
